[83.637255, "o", "a single complete argument, flag + value).\r\n\r\n**Filter used**\r\n\r\n```\r\n[.[] | select(.status == \"active\")\r\n | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email,\r\n    last_login: (.last_login | .[0:10]), role_count: (.roles | length),\r\n    primary_role: (if (.roles | length) > 0 then .roles[0] else null end)}]\r\n| sort_by(.username)\r\n```\r\n\r\nDate formatting uses `.[0:10]` rather than `fromdateiso8601` because jq 1.6 rejects the input's fractional-second timestamps (`...T15:06:40.723617Z`) — all 500 records have the 27-char `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.ffffffZ` shape, so the slice is exact.\r\n\r\n**Checks run**\r\n\r\n- `sh /app/cmd.sh` regenerates the file (rc=0); the harness command form `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' ...) \"$(yq -r '.filter' ...)\" /app/users.json > ...` produces byte-identical output to `cmd.sh` (diff clean).\r\n- Output assertions pass: 346 records, all `last_login` match `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`, every record has exactly the six keys in order, `primary_role` is a string when `role_count > 0` and JSON `null` when `role_c"]
[83.637264, "o", "ount == 0`, and the username list equals its sorted self.\r\n- Spot-checked records: id 2 (`garzaanthony`, 3 roles, `analyst`) and id 6 (`dudleynicholas`, empty roles → `null`).\r\n\r\nNothing is left undone. Note the `status` field also contains `pending` values in the source; those are correctly excluded, since the filter matches `active` exactly.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=12 surface=59338fa2ec97\r\n"]
